# Coding conventions

- C++17; catch exceptions at the plugin boundary (`main.cpp`) — none across the X-Plane boundary
- No exceptions in destructors
- X-Plane API **only** on the main thread
- Inference / network / heavy work on `std::thread` + `std::atomic` status
- Logging: `XPLMDebugString` → Log.txt — **ASCII only** (0x20–0x7E); UTF-8 becomes `?` in Log + ImGui
- JSON: `nlohmann::json`
- Self-contained module headers; no circular includes
- Includes with subdir prefix: `#include "backends/whisper_stt.hpp"`
- Prefer `make format` / `make lint` / `make` over ad-hoc toolchains
- Shallow nesting: early returns and helpers over deep `if`/`switch`
- Clean code: readable names, small functions, no speculative abstractions
- Engine OBJECT lib (`xp_atc_engine`) must stay SDK-free — any TU that includes `<XPLM*.h>` belongs in the plugin module
